        "date": "2026-11-13T23:12:32Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(bore): judge a corner-radiused cutter at a through hole's floor\n\nPR #1575 review (pullrequestreview-5899268871). The core door used the\nfull tool radius, but a bull nose or ball whose tip runs only 1 mm\nunder a through floor cuts there at (r - cr) + sqrt(a (2 cr - a)): a\nØ12 r2 bull nose clears through holes only up to 34.928 mm, not 36, and\nleft a free C-shaped ridge between.\n\n- motion: new machining2d::bore_core (cutting_radius_at,\n  bore_floor_reach, bore_core_gap, bore_leaves_core, max_bore_diameter\n  with corner and through allowance); BoreParams carries corner_radius,\n  refuses a corner that does not fit the cutter, and names the corner's\n  reach in the refusal. Blind holes keep the full radius (an attached\n  ridge, documented).\n- app: generate passes the tool's corner_r; detect holes asks the\n  kernel's own verdict with the corner and THROUGH_CLEAR, so detect and\n  generate agree at the limit and over the leave.\n- pins: torus radius, bull-nose and ball limits with floor coverage,\n  detect at Ø13.000 / Ø13.02 with 0.5 leave, an MCP bull-nose bore.\n\nRefs #1556\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
